# Windsurf Rules: Anti-AI Slop & Authentic UI Craft

You are building production web interfaces. Apply these constraints strictly:

1. COLOUR & PALETTE:
- Select ONE accent colour (<10% of total surface area).
- Neutrals must use a single temperature family (all warm or all cool).
- Strictly ban blue→purple and indigo→violet gradients across buttons, backgrounds, headings, and blobs.
- Strictly ban gradient text (`background-clip: text`).
- Feature grids share uniform card backgrounds and border colours; no rainbow palettes.

2. SURFACES & SHADOWS:
- No drop-shadows on cards, containers, inputs, or buttons.
- Shadows permitted ONLY on floating overlays (modals, popovers, dropdowns, toasts). Keep them tight and low-opacity (`0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)`).
- Prefer whitespace > 1px border > subtle background step for block separation.
- Consistent border-radius and border colour throughout the UI.

3. ICONS & EMOJI:
- Banned: sparkle icons (`✨`, `✦`, `✧`, `🪄`) and AI shimmer glyphs.
- Banned: emoji as UI components (🚀, ⚡, 🎯, 🔥).
- Banned: tinted rounded squares or chip wrappers around icons. Icons sit directly on the background at text size.
- One monochrome icon set inheriting currentColor.

4. COPYWRITING & TYPOGRAPHY:
- Banned buzzwords: unleash, supercharge, elevate, transform, revolutionise, empower, seamless, effortless, cutting-edge, game-changing, next-level, unlock, harness, robust, leverage, powerful, delve.
- Banned: em dash (—) in UI copy.
- Write concrete, specific nouns and numbers.
- Scale: 12 / 14 / 16 / 20 / 24 / 32 / 48px. Sentence case headings and buttons.

5. MOTION & SIZING:
- Hover states change background or border colour only (120-160ms ease-out). No glow, lift, or scale > 1.02.
- Hero text 40-56px desktop. Section padding 64-96px desktop. 4px spatial rhythm.
- No 100vh forced hero traps.

6. CRAFT & A11Y:
- Semantic HTML tags only. Clickable divs are forbidden.
- Clear :focus-visible outlines. Contrast >= 4.5:1.
- CSS Logical Properties (margin-inline-start, padding-inline-end, text-align: start) for internationalization (RTL/LTR).
